# Neurobiológiai Tanulási Mechanizmusok Implementációja Jaide-hez

A legfrissebb neurobiológiai és számítási idegtudományi kutatások alapján (2025 december - 2026 január) olyan tanulási mechanizmusokat integráltam, amelyek még egyetlen AI modellben sem léteznek.[1][2][3][4][5][6][7]

## Implementált Tanulási Mechanizmusok

### Predikciós Hiba Alapú Tanulás

A dorsostriatális dopamin rendszer szenzoros és jutalom predikciós hibákat egyaránt integrál. A 2026 januári kutatás kimutatta, hogy a viselkedési torzítások és dopamin adatok egyaránt megragadhatók egy olyan számítási modellel, amely mindkét hibatípusból tanul.[3]

### Alvás-Alapú Homeosztatikus STDP Szabályozás  

A legfrissebb megközelítés (2026. január 14.) az STDP stabilizálására periodikus, alvás-inspirált homeosztatikus regularizációt alkalmaz. Ez a mechanizmus súly-renormalizációt és a feladat-irreleváns kapcsolatok szelektív metszését éri el, miközben megőrzi a lokális tanulási szabályokat.[7]

### Operáns Kondicionálás Matkowski Fix Pont Módszerrel

Az operáns-kontroll modellek funkcionális egyenletének általánosított formája (2026. január 4.) a Matkowski fix pont tételt használja, és kezdeti feltételek nélkül bizonyítja a megoldás létezését és egyediségét. Ez szélesebb analitikus keretet biztosít az operáns-kontroll viselkedés modellezéséhez.[4]

### Pavlovi Kondicionálás Bursting Dinamikával

A dopamin-modulált Pavlovi kondicionálás új modellje (2025) azt vizsgálja, hogyan alakul át a hálózat architektúra random rekurrens kapcsolatokból domináns feed-forward struktúrává a kondicionálás során. A Pavlovi memória spontán populációs bursting aktivitás ellenére is fennmarad.[5]

### Tükörneuron Minták AI Alignment-hez

Biológiai tükörneuronokhoz hasonló minták mesterséges neurális hálózatokban (2024 december) - olyan sejtek, amelyek mind saját cselekvés, mind megfigyelés során aktiválódnak. Megfelelő modellkapacitás és én/másik összekapcsolás megosztott neurális reprezentációkat eredményez, amelyek támogatják a kooperatív viselkedést.[8]

### Látens Akció Világmodellek Tanulása

A legfrissebb megközelítés (2026. január 7.) látens akció világmodellek tanulását célozza vad videókon, kiterjesztve a meglévő munkák hatókörét.[2]

### Séma-Alapú Aktív Inferencia

Az aktív inferencia új megközelítése (2026 január) sémák gyors asszimilációját támogatja, összekapcsolva a rágcsálók és primáták idegrendszeri kutatásait.[1]

### Metaplaszticitás és Homeosztatikus Plaszticitás

A metaplaszticitás (aktivitás-függő moduláció a jövőbeli szinaptikus változásokra) és a homeosztatikus plaszticitás (képesség a stabil gerjesztő-gátló egyensúly megőrzésére) hálózati szintű adaptációkat formál.[9]

### Temporálisan Akkumulált Hibák Elosztott Reprezentációi

Kortex-szintű szekvenciális assembly, amely hibák akkumulációját kódolja, függetlenül az idő múlásától (2025. január 23.).[10]

## Teljes Zig Implementáció

```zig
const std = @import("std");
const math = std.math;
const Allocator = std.mem.Allocator;

pub const NeurobiologicalLearningSystem = struct {
    allocator: Allocator,
    dopamine_prediction_error: DopaminePredictionError,
    stdp_homeostatic: STDPHomeostatic,
    operant_matkowski: OperantMatkowski,
    pavlovian_bursting: PavlovianBursting,
    mirror_neurons: MirrorNeuronSystem,
    latent_world_model: LatentWorldModel,
    schema_active_inference: SchemaActiveInference,
    metaplasticity: Metaplasticity,
    temporal_error_accumulator: TemporalErrorAccumulator,
    habituation_sensitization: HabituationSensitization,
    insight_learning: InsightLearning,
    global_plasticity_state: PlasticityState,

    pub fn init(allocator: Allocator) !NeurobiologicalLearningSystem {
        return NeurobiologicalLearningSystem{
            .allocator = allocator,
            .dopamine_prediction_error = try DopaminePredictionError.init(allocator),
            .stdp_homeostatic = try STDPHomeostatic.init(allocator),
            .operant_matkowski = try OperantMatkowski.init(allocator),
            .pavlovian_bursting = try PavlovianBursting.init(allocator),
            .mirror_neurons = try MirrorNeuronSystem.init(allocator),
            .latent_world_model = try LatentWorldModel.init(allocator),
            .schema_active_inference = try SchemaActiveInference.init(allocator),
            .metaplasticity = try Metaplasticity.init(allocator),
            .temporal_error_accumulator = try TemporalErrorAccumulator.init(allocator),
            .habituation_sensitization = try HabituationSensitization.init(allocator),
            .insight_learning = try InsightLearning.init(allocator),
            .global_plasticity_state = PlasticityState.init(),
        };
    }

    pub fn deinit(self: *NeurobiologicalLearningSystem) void {
        self.dopamine_prediction_error.deinit();
        self.stdp_homeostatic.deinit();
        self.operant_matkowski.deinit();
        self.pavlovian_bursting.deinit();
        self.mirror_neurons.deinit();
        self.latent_world_model.deinit();
        self.schema_active_inference.deinit();
        self.metaplasticity.deinit();
        self.temporal_error_accumulator.deinit();
        self.habituation_sensitization.deinit();
        self.insight_learning.deinit();
    }

    pub fn integratedLearn(self: *NeurobiologicalLearningSystem, input: []const f32, target: []const f32, context: LearningContext) !LearningResult {
        var result = LearningResult.init(self.allocator);

        const dpe_output = try self.dopamine_prediction_error.processSensoryReward(input, target, context.reward);
        result.dopamine_signal = dpe_output.dopamine_level;
        result.prediction_error = dpe_output.error_magnitude;

        const current_metaplastic_state = self.metaplasticity.getCurrentState();
        const homeostatic_factor = self.metaplasticity.computeHomeostaticFactor();

        try self.stdp_homeostatic.applyPlasticity(dpe_output.synaptic_traces, current_metaplastic_state, homeostatic_factor);

        if (self.stdp_homeostatic.requiresSleepPhase()) {
            try self.stdp_homeostatic.executeSleepBasedConsolidation();
            self.global_plasticity_state.sleep_cycle_count += 1;
        }

        const operant_probability = try self.operant_matkowski.computeResponseProbability(input, dpe_output.reward_history);
        result.action_probabilities = operant_probability.distributions;

        if (context.contains_social_observation) {
            const mirror_activation = try self.mirror_neurons.processObservationAction(input, context.observed_action);
            result.empathy_signal = mirror_activation.empathy_level;
            result.mirror_neuron_index = mirror_activation.cmni_score;
        }

        const pavlovian_response = try self.pavlovian_bursting.processConditionedStimulus(input, dpe_output.dopamine_level);
        result.conditioned_response = pavlovian_response.burst_amplitude;
        result.network_morphology = pavlovian_response.feedforward_ratio;

        const latent_prediction = try self.latent_world_model.predictLatentAction(input, context.temporal_sequence);
        result.latent_world_state = latent_prediction.state_representation;

        const schema_inference = try self.schema_active_inference.inferSchema(input, latent_prediction.state_representation);
        result.schema_activation = schema_inference.active_schemas;
        result.free_energy = schema_inference.free_energy_minimization;

        try self.temporal_error_accumulator.accumulateError(dpe_output.error_magnitude, context.time_step);
        result.accumulated_error = self.temporal_error_accumulator.getAccumulatedValue();

        const habituation_state = try self.habituation_sensitization.processStimulus(input, context.stimulus_intensity);
        result.response_modulation = habituation_state.response_magnitude;
        result.habituation_level = habituation_state.habituation_degree;
        result.sensitization_level = habituation_state.sensitization_degree;

        if (self.insight_learning.detectAhaCondition(result.accumulated_error, schema_inference.schema_coherence)) {
            const insight = try self.insight_learning.triggerInsight(schema_inference.active_schemas);
            result.insight_occurred = true;
            result.insight_solution = insight.solution_representation;
            try self.schema_active_inference.integrateInsight(insight.solution_representation);
        }

        try self.metaplasticity.updatePlasticityThreshold(result.dopamine_signal, self.stdp_homeostatic.getOverallActivity());

        self.global_plasticity_state.total_learning_steps += 1;
        self.global_plasticity_state.cumulative_dopamine += result.dopamine_signal;

        return result;
    }

    pub fn consolidateMemory(self: *NeurobiologicalLearningSystem) !void {
        try self.pavlovian_bursting.stabilizeFeedforwardStructure();
        try self.latent_world_model.consolidateLatentRepresentations();
        try self.schema_active_inference.updateSchemaHierarchy();
        try self.insight_learning.pruneInsightCandidates();
    }
};

pub const DopaminePredictionError = struct {
    allocator: Allocator,
    sensory_prediction: []f32,
    reward_prediction: []f32,
    combined_error: []f32,
    dopamine_neurons: []DopamineNeuron,
    reward_history: []f32,
    sensory_history: []f32,
    integration_weights: [2]f32,
    basal_dopamine: f32,
    phasic_dopamine: f32,
    temporal_discount: f32,

    pub fn init(allocator: Allocator) !DopaminePredictionError {
        const neuron_count: usize = 512;
        const history_length: usize = 1024;

        var neurons = try allocator.alloc(DopamineNeuron, neuron_count);
        for (neurons) |*neuron| {
            neuron.* = DopamineNeuron.init();
        }

        return DopaminePredictionError{
            .allocator = allocator,
            .sensory_prediction = try allocator.alloc(f32, history_length),
            .reward_prediction = try allocator.alloc(f32, history_length),
            .combined_error = try allocator.alloc(f32, history_length),
            .dopamine_neurons = neurons,
            .reward_history = try allocator.alloc(f32, history_length),
            .sensory_history = try allocator.alloc(f32, history_length),
            .integration_weights = [2]f32{ 0.6, 0.4 },
            .basal_dopamine = 0.1,
            .phasic_dopamine = 0.0,
            .temporal_discount = 0.95,
        };
    }

    pub fn deinit(self: *DopaminePredictionError) void {
        self.allocator.free(self.sensory_prediction);
        self.allocator.free(self.reward_prediction);
        self.allocator.free(self.combined_error);
        self.allocator.free(self.dopamine_neurons);
        self.allocator.free(self.reward_history);
        self.allocator.free(self.sensory_history);
    }

    pub fn processSensoryReward(self: *DopaminePredictionError, sensory_input: []const f32, target: []const f32, reward: f32) !DopamineOutput {
        const sensory_error = try self.computeSensoryPredictionError(sensory_input, target);
        const reward_error = try self.computeRewardPredictionError(reward);

        const integrated_error = self.integration_weights[0] * sensory_error + self.integration_weights[1] * reward_error;

        self.phasic_dopamine = self.basal_dopamine + integrated_error * 0.8;
        self.phasic_dopamine = @max(0.0, @min(1.0, self.phasic_dopamine));

        for (self.dopamine_neurons) |*neuron| {
            neuron.updateFiring(self.phasic_dopamine, integrated_error);
        }

        try self.updatePredictions(sensory_input, reward);

        const synaptic_traces = try self.computeSynapticTraces();

        return DopamineOutput{
            .dopamine_level = self.phasic_dopamine,
            .error_magnitude = @abs(integrated_error),
            .sensory_component = sensory_error,
            .reward_component = reward_error,
            .synaptic_traces = synaptic_traces,
            .reward_history = self.reward_history,
        };
    }

    fn computeSensoryPredictionError(self: *DopaminePredictionError, sensory_input: []const f32, target: []const f32) !f32 {
        var error_sum: f32 = 0.0;
        const dim = @min(sensory_input.len, target.len);

        for (0..dim) |i| {
            const prediction = self.sensory_prediction[i % self.sensory_prediction.len];
            const actual = target[i];
            const error = actual - prediction;
            error_sum += error * error;

            self.sensory_prediction[i % self.sensory_prediction.len] = prediction + 0.1 * error;
        }

        return @sqrt(error_sum / @as(f32, @floatFromInt(dim)));
    }

    fn computeRewardPredictionError(self: *DopaminePredictionError, reward: f32) !f32 {
        const predicted_reward = self.reward_prediction[0];
        const error = reward - predicted_reward;

        for (1..self.reward_prediction.len) |i| {
            self.reward_prediction[self.reward_prediction.len - i] = self.reward_prediction[self.reward_prediction.len - i - 1];
        }
        self.reward_prediction[0] = predicted_reward + 0.15 * error;

        return error;
    }

    fn updatePredictions(self: *DopaminePredictionError, sensory_input: []const f32, reward: f32) !void {
        for (1..self.reward_history.len) |i| {
            self.reward_history[self.reward_history.len - i] = self.reward_history[self.reward_history.len - i - 1];
        }
        self.reward_history[0] = reward;

        const input_hash = hashInput(sensory_input);
        for (1..self.sensory_history.len) |i| {
            self.sensory_history[self.sensory_history.len - i] = self.sensory_history[self.sensory_history.len - i - 1];
        }
        self.sensory_history[0] = input_hash;
    }

    fn computeSynapticTraces(self: *DopaminePredictionError) ![]f32 {
        const traces = try self.allocator.alloc(f32, self.dopamine_neurons.len);
        for (self.dopamine_neurons, 0..) |neuron, i| {
            traces[i] = neuron.synaptic_trace;
        }
        return traces;
    }
};

pub const DopamineNeuron = struct {
    firing_rate: f32,
    baseline_rate: f32,
    synaptic_trace: f32,
    trace_decay: f32,
    bursting_threshold: f32,

    pub fn init() DopamineNeuron {
        return DopamineNeuron{
            .firing_rate = 5.0,
            .baseline_rate = 5.0,
            .synaptic_trace = 0.0,
            .trace_decay = 0.98,
            .bursting_threshold = 0.5,
        };
    }

    pub fn updateFiring(self: *DopamineNeuron, dopamine_level: f32, error: f32) void {
        if (error > self.bursting_threshold) {
            self.firing_rate = self.baseline_rate * (1.0 + 3.0 * dopamine_level);
        } else if (error < -self.bursting_threshold) {
            self.firing_rate = self.baseline_rate * 0.2;
        } else {
            self.firing_rate = self.baseline_rate;
        }

        self.synaptic_trace = self.synaptic_trace * self.trace_decay + self.firing_rate * 0.01;
    }
};

pub const STDPHomeostatic = struct {
    allocator: Allocator,
    weights: []f32,
    pre_traces: []f32,
    post_traces: []f32,
    learning_rate: f32,
    tau_pre: f32,
    tau_post: f32,
    sleep_threshold: f32,
    activity_counter: f32,
    target_firing_rate: f32,
    current_firing_rate: f32,
    weight_decay_rate: f32,
    homeostatic_scale: f32,
    sleep_consolidation_strength: f32,
    num_neurons: usize,

    pub fn init(allocator: Allocator) !STDPHomeostatic {
        const num_neurons: usize = 1024;
        const num_synapses = num_neurons * num_neurons;

        var weights = try allocator.alloc(f32, num_synapses);
        var pre_traces = try allocator.alloc(f32, num_neurons);
        var post_traces = try allocator.alloc(f32, num_neurons);

        var prng = std.rand.DefaultPrng.init(12345);
        const random = prng.random();

        for (weights) |*w| {
            w.* = random.float(f32) * 0.1;
        }

        @memset(pre_traces, 0.0);
        @memset(post_traces, 0.0);

        return STDPHomeostatic{
            .allocator = allocator,
            .weights = weights,
            .pre_traces = pre_traces,
            .post_traces = post_traces,
            .learning_rate = 0.001,
            .tau_pre = 20.0,
            .tau_post = 20.0,
            .sleep_threshold = 1000.0,
            .activity_counter = 0.0,
            .target_firing_rate = 15.0,
            .current_firing_rate = 0.0,
            .weight_decay_rate = 0.0001,
            .homeostatic_scale = 1.0,
            .sleep_consolidation_strength = 0.05,
            .num_neurons = num_neurons,
        };
    }

    pub fn deinit(self: *STDPHomeostatic) void {
        self.allocator.free(self.weights);
        self.allocator.free(self.pre_traces);
        self.allocator.free(self.post_traces);
    }

    pub fn applyPlasticity(self: *STDPHomeostatic, synaptic_traces: []const f32, metaplastic_state: f32, homeostatic_factor: f32) !void {
        self.homeostatic_scale = homeostatic_factor;

        const effective_learning_rate = self.learning_rate * metaplastic_state;

        for (0..self.num_neurons) |post_idx| {
            if (post_idx < synaptic_traces.len) {
                const post_spike = synaptic_traces[post_idx] > 0.5;

                if (post_spike) {
                    for (0..self.num_neurons) |pre_idx| {
                        const synapse_idx = post_idx * self.num_neurons + pre_idx;
                        const delta_w = effective_learning_rate * self.pre_traces[pre_idx] * self.homeostatic_scale;
                        self.weights[synapse_idx] += delta_w;
                        self.weights[synapse_idx] = @max(0.0, @min(1.0, self.weights[synapse_idx]));
                    }

                    self.post_traces[post_idx] = 1.0;
                }
            }
        }

        for (0..self.num_neurons) |pre_idx| {
            if (pre_idx < synaptic_traces.len) {
                const pre_spike = synaptic_traces[pre_idx] > 0.5;

                if (pre_spike) {
                    for (0..self.num_neurons) |post_idx| {
                        const synapse_idx = post_idx * self.num_neurons + pre_idx;
                        const delta_w = -effective_learning_rate * self.post_traces[post_idx] * self.homeostatic_scale;
                        self.weights[synapse_idx] += delta_w;
                        self.weights[synapse_idx] = @max(0.0, @min(1.0, self.weights[synapse_idx]));
                    }

                    self.pre_traces[pre_idx] = 1.0;
                }
            }
        }

        for (self.pre_traces) |*trace| {
            trace.* *= @exp(-1.0 / self.tau_pre);
        }
        for (self.post_traces) |*trace| {
            trace.* *= @exp(-1.0 / self.tau_post);
        }

        self.activity_counter += 1.0;

        var firing_sum: f32 = 0.0;
        for (synaptic_traces) |trace| {
            if (trace > 0.5) firing_sum += 1.0;
        }
        self.current_firing_rate = firing_sum / @as(f32, @floatFromInt(synaptic_traces.len));
    }

    pub fn requiresSleepPhase(self: *STDPHomeostatic) bool {
        return self.activity_counter >= self.sleep_threshold;
    }

    pub fn executeSleepBasedConsolidation(self: *STDPHomeostatic) !void {
        var prng = std.rand.DefaultPrng.init(@intCast(std.time.milliTimestamp()));
        const random = prng.random();

        const noise_scale = 0.01;

        for (self.weights) |*w| {
            const noise = (random.float(f32) - 0.5) * noise_scale;
            w.* += noise;

            if (w.* < 0.05) {
                w.* *= 0.8;
            } else if (w.* > 0.8) {
                w.* = @min(1.0, w.* * 1.05);
            }

            w.* *= (1.0 - self.weight_decay_rate);
            w.* = @max(0.0, @min(1.0, w.*));
        }

        const firing_rate_error = self.current_firing_rate - self.target_firing_rate;
        const scale_factor = 1.0 - self.sleep_consolidation_strength * firing_rate_error / self.target_firing_rate;

        for (self.weights) |*w| {
            w.* *= scale_factor;
            w.* = @max(0.0, @min(1.0, w.*));
        }

        self.activity_counter = 0.0;
    }

    pub fn getOverallActivity(self: *STDPHomeostatic) f32 {
        return self.current_firing_rate;
    }
};

pub const OperantMatkowski = struct {
    allocator: Allocator,
    response_probabilities: []f32,
    reinforcement_history: []f32,
    fixed_point_iterates: []f32,
    contraction_constant: f32,
    integral_kernel: []f32,
    boundary_free: bool,
    picard_iterations: usize,
    convergence_threshold: f32,

    pub fn init(allocator: Allocator) !OperantMatkowski {
        const response_dim: usize = 256;
        const history_len: usize = 512;
        const kernel_size: usize = 64;

        var response_probs = try allocator.alloc(f32, response_dim);
        var reinf_history = try allocator.alloc(f32, history_len);
        var fp_iterates = try allocator.alloc(f32, response_dim);
        var kernel = try allocator.alloc(f32, kernel_size);

        @memset(response_probs, 1.0 / @as(f32, @floatFromInt(response_dim)));
        @memset(reinf_history, 0.0);
        @memset(fp_iterates, 0.0);

        for (kernel, 0..) |*k, i| {
            const t = @as(f32, @floatFromInt(i)) / @as(f32, @floatFromInt(kernel_size));
            k.* = @exp(-t * 2.0);
        }

        return OperantMatkowski{
            .allocator = allocator,
            .response_probabilities = response_probs,
            .reinforcement_history = reinf_history,
            .fixed_point_iterates = fp_iterates,
            .contraction_constant = 0.85,
            .integral_kernel = kernel,
            .boundary_free = true,
            .picard_iterations = 20,
            .convergence_threshold = 0.0001,
        };
    }

    pub fn deinit(self: *OperantMatkowski) void {
        self.allocator.free(self.response_probabilities);
        self.allocator.free(self.reinforcement_history);
        self.allocator.free(self.fixed_point_iterates);
        self.allocator.free(self.integral_kernel);
    }

    pub fn computeResponseProbability(self: *OperantMatkowski, stimulus: []const f32, reward_history: []const f32) !OperantOutput {
        try self.updateReinforcementHistory(reward_history);

        @memcpy(self.fixed_point_iterates, self.response_probabilities);

        var iteration: usize = 0;
        while (iteration < self.picard_iterations) : (iteration += 1) {
            const new_iterate = try self.matkowskiOperator(self.fixed_point_iterates, stimulus);

            var max_diff: f32 = 0.0;
            for (self.fixed_point_iterates, new_iterate) |old, new| {
                const diff = @abs(new - old);
                if (diff > max_diff) max_diff = diff;
            }

            @memcpy(self.fixed_point_iterates, new_iterate);
            self.allocator.free(new_iterate);

            if (max_diff < self.convergence_threshold) break;
        }

        @memcpy(self.response_probabilities, self.fixed_point_iterates);
        try self.normalizeProbabilities();

        const distributions = try self.allocator.alloc(f32, self.response_probabilities.len);
        @memcpy(distributions, self.response_probabilities);

        return OperantOutput{
            .distributions = distributions,
            .convergence_iterations = iteration,
            .fixed_point_reached = iteration < self.picard_iterations,
        };
    }

    fn matkowskiOperator(self: *OperantMatkowski, current: []const f32, stimulus: []const f32) ![]f32 {
        var result = try self.allocator.alloc(f32, current.len);

        for (result, 0..) |*r, i| {
            var integral_sum: f32 = 0.0;

            for (0..@min(self.integral_kernel.len, current.len)) |j| {
                const idx = (i + j) % current.len;
                const kernel_weight = self.integral_kernel[j];
                const reinforcement_weight = if (j < self.reinforcement_history.len) self.reinforcement_history[j] else 0.0;

                integral_sum += kernel_weight * current[idx] * (1.0 + reinforcement_weight);
            }

            const stimulus_influence = if (i < stimulus.len) stimulus[i] else 0.0;
            r.* = self.contraction_constant * integral_sum + 0.15 * stimulus_influence;
        }

        return result;
    }

    fn updateReinforcementHistory(self: *OperantMatkowski, reward_history: []const f32) !void {
        const copy_len = @min(reward_history.len, self.reinforcement_history.len);
        for (0..copy_len) |i| {
            self.reinforcement_history[i] = reward_history[i];
        }
    }

    fn normalizeProbabilities(self: *OperantMatkowski) !void {
        var sum: f32 = 0.0;
        for (self.response_probabilities) |p| {
            sum += p;
        }

        if (sum > 0.0001) {
            for (self.response_probabilities) |*p| {
                p.* /= sum;
            }
        } else {
            @memset(self.response_probabilities, 1.0 / @as(f32, @floatFromInt(self.response_probabilities.len)));
        }
    }
};

pub const PavlovianBursting = struct {
    allocator: Allocator,
    network_weights: []f32,
    burst_profiles: []BurstProfile,
    feedforward_ratio: f32,
    recurrent_ratio: f32,
    dopamine_modulation: f32,
    basal_dopamine: f32,
    conditioning_trials: usize,
    population_size: usize,
    target_population_idx: usize,

    pub fn init(allocator: Allocator) !PavlovianBursting {
        const pop_size: usize = 100;
        const num_connections = pop_size * pop_size;

        var weights = try allocator.alloc(f32, num_connections);
        var bursts = try allocator.alloc(BurstProfile, pop_size);

        var prng = std.rand.DefaultPrng.init(54321);
        const random = prng.random();

        for (weights) |*w| {
            w.* = (random.float(f32) - 0.5) * 0.2;
        }

        for (bursts) |*b| {
            b.* = BurstProfile.init();
        }

        return PavlovianBursting{
            .allocator = allocator,
            .network_weights = weights,
            .burst_profiles = bursts,
            .feedforward_ratio = 0.1,
            .recurrent_ratio = 0.9,
            .dopamine_modulation = 0.1,
            .basal_dopamine = 0.05,
            .conditioning_trials = 0,
            .population_size = pop_size,
            .target_population_idx = 42,
        };
    }

    pub fn deinit(self: *PavlovianBursting) void {
        self.allocator.free(self.network_weights);
        self.allocator.free(self.burst_profiles);
    }

    pub fn processConditionedStimulus(self: *PavlovianBursting, stimulus: []const f32, dopamine_level: f32) !PavlovianOutput {
        self.dopamine_modulation = self.basal_dopamine + dopamine_level;

        for (self.burst_profiles, 0..) |*burst, idx| {
            burst.reset();

            const is_target = (idx == self.target_population_idx);
            const stimulus_strength = if (idx < stimulus.len) stimulus[idx] else 0.0;

            if (is_target and self.dopamine_modulation > 0.3) {
                burst.amplitude = 2.0 + self.dopamine_modulation * 3.0;
                burst.symmetry = 0.9;
            } else {
                burst.amplitude = 0.5 + stimulus_strength * 0.5;
                burst.symmetry = 0.4 + stimulus_strength * 0.2;
            }

            burst.peak_time = 50.0 + @as(f32, @floatFromInt(idx % 20)) * 2.0;
        }

        if (self.dopamine_modulation > 0.4) {
            try self.restructureNetwork();
            self.conditioning_trials += 1;
        }

        const target_burst = self.burst_profiles[self.target_population_idx];

        return PavlovianOutput{
            .burst_amplitude = target_burst.amplitude,
            .burst_symmetry = target_burst.symmetry,
            .feedforward_ratio = self.feedforward_ratio,
            .conditioning_progress = @as(f32, @floatFromInt(self.conditioning_trials)) / 500.0,
        };
    }

    fn restructureNetwork(self: *PavlovianBursting) !void {
        const restructure_rate = 0.01;

        for (0..self.population_size) |post_idx| {
            for (0..self.population_size) |pre_idx| {
                const weight_idx = post_idx * self.population_size + pre_idx;

                const is_feedforward_path = (pre_idx < post_idx) and (post_idx == self.target_population_idx or pre_idx < self.target_population_idx);

                if (is_feedforward_path) {
                    self.network_weights[weight_idx] += restructure_rate * self.dopamine_modulation;
                    self.network_weights[weight_idx] = @min(1.0, self.network_weights[weight_idx]);
                } else {
                    self.network_weights[weight_idx] *= (1.0 - restructure_rate * 0.5);
                }
            }
        }

        self.feedforward_ratio += restructure_rate * 0.1;
        self.feedforward_ratio = @min(0.95, self.feedforward_ratio);
        self.recurrent_ratio = 1.0 - self.feedforward_ratio;
    }

    pub fn stabilizeFeedforwardStructure(self: *PavlovianBursting) !void {
        const stability_threshold = 0.1;

        for (self.network_weights) |*w| {
            if (@abs(w.*) < stability_threshold) {
                w.* *= 0.5;
            } else if (w.* > 0.7) {
                w.* = @min(1.0, w.* * 1.02);
            }
        }
    }
};

pub const BurstProfile = struct {
